<title>FRANCE: No word on CIC tender expected Monday.</title>
<headline>No word on CIC tender expected Monday.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French finance ministry said no announcement was expected on Monday on the outcome of the tender for the partial privatisation of CIC, the banking arm of state-owned insurer GAN, which closes later in the day.</p>
<p>The tender for the regional banking group expires at 1600 GMT. Ordinarily, announcement of the results is not expected on the same day as the close of the tender.</p>
<p>Some 67 percent of Credit Commercial et Industriel (CIC) bank is being offered for sale.</p>
<p>Groupe des Assurances Nationales (GAN) will keep around 25 percent of the bank. GAN is itself a candidate for sale once CIC is privatised.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
